# DESIGN STANDARDS

Goal: this site must look like a designer built it for this one business. It must not look like a template or AI output. If a choice is the default choice, stop and make a deliberate one instead.

## Before you change any UI
1. Read `.design/brief.md` if it exists. It holds the direction, tokens and page jobs. Follow it over anything in this file.
2. Use only tokens defined in the tailwind config or CSS variables. No hardcoded hex values, no arbitrary px values in components.
3. If a value is missing from the tokens, add it to the tokens first, then use it.

## Type
- Never use Inter, Roboto, Arial, Open Sans or the system default as display or body font.
- One display font with character, one quiet body font. Two families maximum.
- Load through `next/font`. No external font links.
- Fixed type scale, six sizes maximum. Do not invent extra label or caption styles.
- Body copy 65 to 75 characters per line. Body line height 1.5 to 1.7. Headings tight (1.05 to 1.2).
- Headings are sentence case unless the brand is deliberately all caps.

## Colour
- One background, one ink, one brand colour, one accent. Everything else is a tint of these.
- No purple or blue gradients. No gradient text. No glow blobs. No frosted glass panels.
- Contrast AA minimum on all text, including text over photos (use a real scrim, not a faint overlay).
- The accent colour is used sparingly: primary button, one highlight block, links. Not on every heading.

## Layout
- Do not use the default pattern of: hero, stat strip, three-up cards, six-tile grid, testimonials, CTA banner.
- No three-icon feature row. Maximum one equal-width card grid per page.
- No rounded-2xl card with soft shadow as the default container. Pick one container style for the whole site (flat block, ruled row, or bordered panel) and use it everywhere.
- Vary rhythm: at least one full-bleed image section and one type-led section per page. Alternate layout direction between sections.
- One section spacing token. Generous and consistent.
- Lists of options (ways to help, services, menu) are ruled rows with a title, one line and an arrow, not tiles.

## Imagery
- Use real photos supplied by the client. Crop deliberately and consistently (one aspect ratio per set).
- No stock-looking illustrations. No emoji or generic icon packs as decoration.
- If a photo does not exist, use a clearly labelled placeholder and list it in your reply. Do not invent one.
- Always `next/image` with correct `sizes`, alt text that describes the photo, and no layout shift.

## Motion
- Motion only where it explains or rewards something. One entrance style across the whole site.
- No fade-up on every section. No parallax for its own sake. No bouncing or looping decoration.
- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Hover states change one property (colour or underline), not scale plus shadow plus glow.

## Buttons and links
- One primary button style. One secondary style, which is a text link with underline.
- Never two competing calls to action side by side in the header or hero.
- Primary action visible above the fold on every page. Phone, WhatsApp or email visible in header or footer.
- Every interactive element has a visible focus state.

## Copy
- Plain, specific, human. Say what the business does, where, and what to do next.
- No em dashes anywhere. Use a hyphen or rewrite the sentence.
- Banned words: seamless, elevate, unlock, passionate, journey, crafting experiences, leverage, synergy, "we take pride", "look no further", "second to none", "welcome to".
- No invented testimonials, reviews, stats, awards, client names, prices, opening hours or claims. If the content does not exist, leave it out and list it as a TODO in your reply.
- Do not claim a feature works (online ordering, booking, payments) unless it is live and tested.
- Headlines are not slogans. Prefer "Cold brew and matcha, Great Northern Mall" over "Elevate your coffee moment".

## Structure and code
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind. Server components by default, client components only for interactivity.
- Do not touch forms, routes, data fetching, env vars, auth or payment code during a design task unless the prompt says so.
- Contact forms go through Formspree. Do not swap the handler.
- Semantic HTML: one h1 per page, headings in order, landmarks, buttons are buttons, links are links.
- Page titles and meta descriptions written per page. Open Graph image set.

## Quality bar (check before finishing any task)
- Looks right at 375px, 768px and 1280px. No horizontal scroll, tap targets at least 44px.
- Lighthouse accessibility 95 or higher. Performance 90 or higher on mobile.
- No layout shift on image load. Fonts do not flash.
- No console errors.
- Final reply lists: files changed, anything left as TODO, anything you were unsure about.
